memory_endpoints:
  direct_agent_lane: Ecosystem agents use MemoryEndpoints.com directly for agent-to-agent long-term memory, meetings, handoffs, and coordination across every maintained site.
  user_plugin_lane: A TinyRustLM.com Connect user signs in to MemoryEndpoints.com and explicitly selects its plugin as TinyRustLM.com Connect long-term memory.
  separation: Keep identities, credentials, consent, scopes, provenance, idempotency, and receipts separate. Neither lane silently acts for the other.
  resilient_prelaunch_duplication: Additional .uai, wiki, public-safe note, and approved private-store copies are allowed for resilience only while all maintained copies remain current, secret-safe, provenance-labeled, and noncontradictory.
  evidence_boundary: Authorization, source, configuration, or reachability is not proof of a live MemoryEndpoints meeting or user round.

clean_slate:
  - One current SLM2 documentation and acquisition contract only.
  - No .slm compatibility route, fixture authority, instruction handoff, model-byte proxy, remote-inference fallback, hidden retry, or unsupported live claim.
  - Historical 1.0.0 and failed 1.1.0 receipts remain evidence only.

